<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tormes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tormes is a river of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> that rises in the Sierra de Gredos and flows north-west through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salamanca">Salamanca</a> to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douro">Duero</a> on the Portuguese border. After Ramiro II's victory at Simancas in 939, the Kingdom of León resettled its valley around Salamanca. The river is also known from the Spanish picaresque novel Lazarillo de Tormes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tormes.jpg" alt="Tormes" width="320" height="199" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Luidger · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20060706-Alba_de_Tormes_edited.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
